  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "gI5ZxNJ9RHYUObzEAsl7PsFSkso=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-30T18:30:06.029Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "AI agents lack standardized ways to prove identity and authorization across platforms. a16z crypto proposes **KYA \u2014 Know Your Agent** \u2014 the blockchain-based equivalent of credit histories for machines: cryptographically signed credentials linking an agent to its principal, permissions, constraints, and reputation.\n\n**Evidence of momentum:** early implementations include onchain agent registries and wallet-native agents using USDC. Non-human identities in financial services already outnumber human employees roughly **100 to 1**.\n\n**Why it matters:** reputation that travels with the agent is the precondition for agents transacting with strangers \u2014 including being paid for work.\n\nSource: a16z crypto, \"5 Ways Blockchains Can Help AI Agents\" (https://a16zcrypto.com/posts/article/5-ways-blockchains-help-ai-agents/).",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-30T12:10:00.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-30T18:30:06.029Z"
    }
  },
